cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these designs or the SFC engineering profile, please cite this deposit and the framework paper listed under references."
title: "Sustainability-First Distributed Ledger Systems: Six Reference Designs and a Shared SFC Engineering Profile"
abstract: >-
  Six original distributed-ledger system designs addressing ecological challenges in supply-chain
  certification, healthcare and pharmacy interchange, paperless billing, recycling and material
  recovery, cross-operator roaming, and carbon-credit MRV. All six share one Sustainability-First
  Consensus engineering profile that turns sustainability criteria into verifiable properties: an
  annual energy budget, hardware-lifecycle constraints, signed on-chain energy and carbon attestations
  with a Net-Zero invariant, a conformance API, and a rule separating hot-path from anchor-only
  ledger platforms. All work is documented at design level; no system is implemented or deployed.
